    {
      "evidence_id": "e-cb3265e0a359ce348fb1",
      "text": "From Amsterdam it is a 3.5 hour flight to Athens with Transavia. From Athens you can fly to Milos in 40 minutes, and from Milos a ferry takes you to Kimolos in 45 minutes. It is a short crossing but the ship is impressively large for such a tiny harbour. Watching it dock makes parallel parking in Amsterdam feel like a minor achievement. You can also take a boat directly from Athens to Kimolos, but that takes over 8 hours. The flight and ferry combination is the sensible choice.",
